   "text": "The three homes just mentioned present a fascinating story, but there are many other homes as a result of Association work-for old folk, for orphans, for fallen girls, for business girls, telling stories of just plain, hard sacrifice. Mothers' meetings, notable in results at Tuskegee, Louisville, St. Louis, Jacksonville, and at Jackson and Westside, Mississippi, have proven one of the most helpful and interesting features of the movement, and the results have been far-reaching.",
